        "original_id": "48be3595-414b-5980-91e6-d04d1e0821c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Graham Hill, Richie Ginther, Bruce McLaren\n- Events: 1962 Italian Grand Prix, 1963 Lombank Trophy, 2009 Monaco Grand Prix\n- Teams/Constructors: Cooper, BRM\n- Products/Cars: BRM P57\n\nFacts:\n- The 1962 Italian Grand Prix ended with Richie Ginther finishing second and Cooper driver Bruce McLaren finishing third.\n- Norman Graham Hill was born on 15 February 1929 and died on 29 November 1975.\n- Graham Hill was a British racing driver and team owner from England who became a two-time Formula One World Champion.\n- The 1963 Lombank Trophy was run over 50 laps and was won by British driver Graham Hill in a BRM P57.\n- The 2009 Monaco Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 24 May 2009 at the Circuit de Monaco in Monaco.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "574e8242-0658-562f-b346-0b704f393052",
        "text": "Page: 1962 Italian Grand Prix. Sentence: His teammate Richie Ginther finished second and Cooper driver Bruce McLaren came in third.\nPage: Graham Hill. Sentence: Norman Graham Hill {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (15 February 1929 – 29 November 1975) was a British racing driver and team owner from England, who was twice Formula One World Champion.\nPage: 1963 Lombank Trophy. Sentence: The race was run over 50 laps of the circuit, and was won by British driver Graham Hill in a BRM P57.\nPage: 2009 Monaco Grand Prix. Sentence: The 2009 Monaco Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race that was held on 24 May 2009 at the Circuit de Monaco, in Monaco.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
